  "body": "The gamma function  The gamma function is defined by the improper integral We shall now compute for all natural numbers .    To get started, we'll compute   Then compute For the last equality, we used that .  Now we move on to general , using the same type of computation as we just used to evaluate . For any natural number , To get to the third row, we used that .  Now that we know and , for all , we can compute all of the 's. That is, the factorial is just The Gamma function is far more important than just a generalisation of the factorial. It appears all over mathematics, physics, statistics and beyond. It has all sorts of interesting properties and its definition can be extended from natural numbers to all numbers excluding . For example, one can show that  the Gamma function shifted by one.    "
