  "url": "sec_improp_int.html#sec_improp_int-5-12",
  "type": "Proof",
  "number": "1.12.3.1",
  "title": "",
  "body": " By definition the improper integral converges if and only if the limit exists and is finite. (Remember that, in computing the limit, is a finite constant independent of and so can be pulled out of the limit.) But that is the case if and only if the limit exists and is finite, which in turn is the case if and only if the integral converges.  "
