  "body": "Example , continued  Imagine, as in Example , that there are a finite number of masses arrayed along a (vertical) -axis with mass number attached at height . Again, the total mass and centre of mass of the array are Now suppose that we lift, for each , mass number , against gravity, from its initial height to a final height . So after the lift we have a new array of masses with total mass and centre of mass To lift the mass took work . So the total work required to lift all masses was So the work required to lift the array of particles is identical to the work required to lift a single particle, whose mass, , is the total mass of the array, from height , the initial centre of mass of the array, to height , the final centre of mass of the array.  "
