  "body": "Mixing brines  A tank contains 1500 liters of brine with a concentration of kg of salt per liter. Another brine solution, this with a concentration of kg of salt per liter is poured into the tank at a rate of li\/min. At the same time, li\/min of the solution in the tank, which is stirred continuously, is drained from the tank.  How many kilograms of salt will remain in the tank after half an hour?  How long will it take to reduce the concentration to kg\/li?    Solution: Denote by the amount of salt in the tank at time . In a very short time interval , the incoming solution adds liters of a solution carrying kg\/li. So the incoming solution adds kg of salt. In the same time interval liters is drained from the tank. The concentration of the drained brine is . So kg were removed. All together, the change in the salt content of the tank during the short time interval is The rate of change of salt content per unit time is The solution of this equation is by Theorem , with and . At time , . So   (a) At    (b) kg is achieved when   "
