  "body": "An awkward series to test  Comparing the series we see that and does not converge as . Since the limit of the ratios does not exist, we cannot tell anything from the ratio test. Nonetheless, we can still figure out for which 's our power series converges.  Because every coefficient is either 1 or 2, the term in our series obeys and so is smaller than the term in the geometric series . This geometric series converges if . So, by the comparison test, our series converges for too.  Since every is at least one, the term in our series obeys If , this cannot converge to zero as , and our series diverges by the divergence test.  In conclusion, our series converges if and only if , and so has radius of convergence .  "
