  "body": " Optional Another approach to showing that is  We already know from Example , that the series converges to some function for all values of . All that remains to do is to show that is really . We will do this by showing that and satisfy the same differential equation with the same initial conditions Recall that when we solve of a separable differential equation our general solution will have an arbitrary constant in it. That constant cannot be determined from the differential equation alone and we need some extra data to find it. This extra information is often information about the system at its beginning (for example when position or time is zero) hence initial conditions . Of course the reader is already familiar with this because it was covered back in Section . . We know that satisfies and by Theorem (with , and ), this is the only solution. So it suffices to show that satisfies     By Theorem ,   When we substitute into the series we get (see the discussion after Definition )   Hence solves the same initial value problem and we must have .  "
