  "body": "Rational roots of   .  Solution:   The constant term in this polynomial is and the coefficient of the highest power of is .  Thus the only candidates for integer roots are .  By our newest trick, the only candidates for fractional roots are .  We try each in turn Again, this is a little tedious, but not difficult. Its actually pretty easy to code up for a computer to do. Modern polynomial factoring algorithms do more sophisticated things, but these are a pretty good way to start.  so the roots are and .    "
